  "normative_behavior": [
    "The top and bottom toolbar flags are independent persistent site settings.",
    "When the bottom toolbar is enabled, public Wikidot chrome renders #footer-bar with the heading Other interesting sites and promoted-site cards.",
    "Each observed card links to the promoted site in a new browsing context and uses the Wikidot 80px site-thumbnail URL shape.",
    "The footer bar is static document flow, not fixed or sticky. At 479px the four 185px cards wrap into two rows; at 767px and 1280px the observed cards remain in one row.",
    "The promotion control is an independent persistent flag whose own label defines its direction as promoting this site on other sites. The capture does not establish a random-selection algorithm or ordering contract.",
    "A saved toolbar setting and the immediately served public HTML are separate temporal states on legacy Wikidot because its public static cache can retain the previous document after the setting is restored."
  ],
  "non_claims": [
    "No random or weighted promoted-site ordering algorithm was established.",
    "No promise is made that a Wikidot public page reflects a toolbar-setting mutation on the first reload.",
    "The capture establishes a stale-public-document lower bound of 60 seconds after restore, but it does not establish the eventual convergence deadline. Wikijump candidate behavior must therefore be compared as a temporal compatibility surface rather than treating immediate freshness as an automatic improvement."
